signed type, the type is also an assigned id for this element, which means that the type can also be used here.\n                    </p>\n\n                  </div>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">extension\n                  <a name=\"extension-context-type-extension\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Extension URL</td>\n                <td>\n                  <div>\n                    <p>The context is a particular extension from a particular StructureDefinition, and the expression is just a uri that identifies the extension.</p>\n\n                  </div>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
