     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n            <p class=\"res-header-id\">\n              <b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem request-status</b>\n            </p>\n            <a name=\"request-status\"> </a>\n            <a name=\"hcrequest-status\"> </a>\n            <p>This case-sensitive code system \n              <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/request-status</code> defines the following codes in an undefined hierarchy:\n            </p>\n            <table class=\"codes\">\n              <tr>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Lvl</b>\n                </td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">\n                  <b>Code</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Display</b>\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  <b>Definition</b>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">draft\n                  <a name=\"request-status-draft\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Draft</td>\n                <td>The request has been created but is not yet complete or ready for action.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">active\n                  <a name=\"request-status-active\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Active</td>\n                <td>The request is in force and ready to be acted upon.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">on-hold\n                  <a name=\"request-status-on-hold\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>On Hold</td>\n                <td>The request (and any implicit authorization to act) has been temporarily withdrawn but is expected to resume in the future.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">entered-in-error\n                  <a name=\"request-status-entered-in-error\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Entered in Error</td>\n                <td>This request should never have existed and should be considered 'void'.  (It is possible that real-world decisions were based on it.  If real-world activity has occurred, the status should be \"revoked\" rather than \"entered-in-error\".).</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ended\n                  <a name=\"request-status-ended\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Ended</td>\n                <td>This request is no longer to be acted upon. This status does not differentiate what degree of action (if any) has already been undertaken against the request.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>2</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  completed\n                  <a name=\"request-status-completed\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Completed</td>\n                <td>The activity described by the request has been fully performed.  No further activity will occur.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>2</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">  revoked\n                  <a name=\"request-status-revoked\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Revoked</td>\n                <td>The request (and any implicit authorization to act) has been terminated prior to the known full completion of the intended actions.  No further activity should occur.</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td>1</td>\n                <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">unknown\n                  <a name=\"request-status-unknown\"> </a>\n                </td>\n                <td>Unknown</td>\n                <td>The authoring/source system does not